//      span, leaving it open. Fix: Before breaking on EOS inside a constrained span, call
//      CloseSpanWithinBudget(30) to salvage the span from whatever valid prefix was built.
//   2. unterminated_constrained_segment (4 examples): Same EOS-inside-span issue at budget edge.
//      Final cleanup already uses CloseSpanWithinBudget but currentConstrainedOut may be in an
//      awkward partial state. The EOS escape gives a second chance before the cleanup.
//   3. other_observed_failure (22 examples): Semantically wrong but syntactically valid.
//      Better guidance to forbid assignment syntax (=) and comparisons (>, <, ==, >=, <=)
//      inside << >>, which cause EOS selection and/or malformed spans.
//   4. Repetition penalty reduced from 4.0 to 2.0: High penalty over-penalizes correct variable
//      names that appear in the preamble, biasing the model toward alternate (wrong) names.
//
// Unchanged from attempt 2:
